# fixedbugs, defect 2117, 2026-10-17, defect 2049's second shape past 4,096
# bytes.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header declaring `int h_<module>_main(int x);`, the name this
# compiler writes for the program's `main`, on a line past 4,096 bytes was
# told `internal error: compiling the generated C failed` at exit 2: clang
# quotes no such line under its note, and the reader read the name under the
# note's caret in the line clang quoted.
#
# FIX: the name is read from the header's bytes (`cli/caret_bytes.hero`), told
# as the one the C this compiler writes gives the program's `main`, exit 1,
# with a `guess` fix.

extern "fixedbugs-2117-a-header-declaring-main-s-c-name-on-a-line-past-4096-bytes-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
